### 1 · Service dependency map — graph (below left)

**A** is the edges, **B** the per-service error ratio that colours the nodes.

```promql
label_join(
  topk($topk,
    sum by (client, server) (
      rate(traces_service_graph_request_total{client_k8s_cluster_name=~"$cluster", client_k8s_namespace_name=~"$namespace", client=~"$client", server=~"$server", client!="", server!=""}[$__range])
    )
  ),
  "id", "-->", "client", "server"
)
```
`Format: Table` · `Type: Instant`

```promql
label_join(
  (
      sum by (server) (rate(traces_service_graph_request_failed_total{client_k8s_cluster_name=~"$cluster", client_k8s_namespace_name=~"$namespace", client=~"$client", server=~"$server", client!="", server!=""}[$__range]))
    / sum by (server) (rate(traces_service_graph_request_total{client_k8s_cluster_name=~"$cluster", client_k8s_namespace_name=~"$namespace", client=~"$client", server=~"$server", client!="", server!=""}[$__range]))
  )
  and on (server)
  sum by (server) (
    topk($topk,
      sum by (client, server) (
        rate(traces_service_graph_request_total{client_k8s_cluster_name=~"$cluster", client_k8s_namespace_name=~"$namespace", client=~"$client", server=~"$server", client!="", server!=""}[$__range])
      )
    )
  ),
  "id", "", "server"
)
```
`Format: Table` · `Type: Instant` — note `and on (server)`, which keeps the node set to
the services the top-$topk edges actually reach.

Two queries, so the value columns arrive as `Value #A`/`Value #B` and `organize` renames
both to `Value`:

```json
[
  {
    "id": "organize",
    "options": {
      "excludeByName": {
        "Time": true,
        "client": true,
        "server": true
      },
      "indexByName": {
        "id": 0,
        "Value #A": 1,
        "Value #B": 1
      },
      "renameByName": {
        "Value #A": "Value",
        "Value #B": "Value"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "rowsToFields",
    "options": {}
  }
]
```

### 2 · CPU requests: cluster → namespace → workload — sankey (below right)

One query: two levels joined by PromQL `or`. Two queries plus `merge` looks equivalent
and is not — `merge` unifies by field name, so `Value #A`/`Value #B` stay separate and
half the marks come out null.

```promql
label_join(
  topk($topk,
    sum by (cluster, namespace) (
      kube_pod_container_resource_requests{resource="cpu", cluster=~"$cluster", namespace=~"$namespace", cluster!="", namespace!=""}
    )
  ),
  "id", "-->", "cluster", "namespace"
)
  or
label_join(
  topk($topk,
    sum by (namespace, workload) (
      namespace_workload_pod:kube_pod_owner:relabel{namespace=~"$namespace"}
        * on (namespace, pod) group_left()
          sum by (namespace, pod) (
            kube_pod_container_resource_requests{resource="cpu", cluster=~"$cluster", namespace=~"$namespace"}
          )
    )
  ),
  "id", "-->", "namespace", "workload"
)
```

```json
[
  {
    "id": "organize",
    "options": {
      "excludeByName": {
        "Time": true,
        "cluster": true,
        "namespace": true,
        "workload": true
      },
      "indexByName": {
        "id": 0,
        "Value": 1
      },
      "renameByName": {}
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "rowsToFields",
    "options": {}
  }
]
```

### 3 · Service call matrix inside `$namespace` — chord

Both ends scoped to `$namespace`, which is what makes it square.

```promql
label_join(
  topk($topk,
    sum by (client, server) (
      rate(traces_service_graph_request_total{client_k8s_cluster_name=~"$cluster", server_k8s_cluster_name=~"$cluster", client_k8s_namespace_name=~"$namespace", server_k8s_namespace_name=~"$namespace", client!="", server!=""}[$__range])
    )
  ),
  "id", "-->", "client", "server"
)
```

### 4 · The label carrier — graph

`id` is opaque here (`client:server`, no `-->`), and the endpoints ride in
`source`/`target` labels. The query emits `src`/`dst` and `organize` renames them —
emitting `source`/`target` directly would trip the legacy row-format pre-pass.

```promql
label_join(
  label_join(
    label_join(
      topk($topk,
        sum by (client, server) (
          rate(traces_service_graph_request_total{client_k8s_cluster_name=~"$cluster", client_k8s_namespace_name=~"$namespace", client=~"$client", server=~"$server", client!="", server!=""}[$__range])
        )
      ),
      "id", ":", "client", "server"
    ),
    "src", "", "client"
  ),
  "dst", "", "server"
)
```

```json
[
  {
    "id": "organize",
    "options": {
      "excludeByName": {
        "Time": true,
        "client": true,
        "server": true
      },
      "indexByName": {
        "id": 0,
        "Value": 1,
        "src": 2,
        "dst": 3
      },
      "renameByName": {
        "src": "source",
        "dst": "target"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "rowsToFields",
    "options": {}
  }
]
```

